# Copy this file to .env and fill in your OAuth client credentials.
# All values are read at runtime by the Electron main process.
#
# ─── Google (Gmail) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  1. Visit https://console.cloud.google.com → New Project ("MailVault")
#  2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Gmail API"
#  3. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen
#       - User Type: External
#       - Add scopes:
#           gmail.readonly, gmail.modify, gmail.settings.basic
#       - Add YOUR personal email as a Test User
#       - Leave the app in "Testing" status (no verification needed for self-use)
#  4. APIs & Services → Credentials → Create Credentials → OAuth client ID
#       - Application type: Desktop app
#       - Copy the client_id (ends in .apps.googleusercontent.com)  →  VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
#       - Copy the client_secret                                     →  VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
#
#  Note: For Desktop apps the "secret" is not really secret — it's bundled in the binary.
#  Google's token endpoint requires it for app-identification; PKCE protects the auth code itself.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── Microsoft (Hotmail / Outlook / Live) ─────────────────────────────────────
#  1. Visit https://portal.azure.com → Microsoft Entra ID → App Registrations → New
#       - Name: MailVault
#       - Supported account types: "Accounts in any organizational directory and
#         personal Microsoft accounts" (REQUIRED for @hotmail.com / @live.com / @outlook.com)
#       - Redirect URI: under "Mobile and desktop applications" platform, add
#           http://localhost
#         (Microsoft accepts ANY loopback port at runtime when this base is registered.)
#  2. API permissions → Microsoft Graph → Delegated:
#       openid, profile, email, offline_access,
#       Mail.Read, Mail.ReadWrite,
#       MailboxSettings.Read, MailboxSettings.ReadWrite,
#       User.Read
#  3. Do NOT create a client secret — desktop apps use PKCE.
#  4. Copy the Application (client) ID → VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID
VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
